From: Yury Ilyanok <yury.ilyanok@gmail.com>
Subject: net: phy: aquantia: rate-match to a fixed 10GBASE-R host on request

When an AQR113C sits behind a host SerDes that is fixed at 10GBASE-R
(e.g. the RTL9303 switch port on the Verizon CR1000A), its firmware
default of provisioning the sub-10G line rates for USXGMII rate
adaptation cannot work: the host cannot follow the line-rate change, so
a 5G/2.5G/1G client links but passes no traffic.  Re-provision those
rates to 10GBASE-R (XFI) + PAUSE rate matching instead.

Gate the re-provisioning on a new "aquantia,host-10gbase-r-fixed" PHY
node property so only boards that declare the constraint are affected;
PHYs without the property (e.g. the USXGMII-attached WAN AQR113C on the
same board) keep the firmware provisioning.

Signed-off-by: Yury Ilyanok <yury.ilyanok@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia_main.c
@@ -615,6 +615,34 @@
 	if (!ret)
 		aqr107_chip_info(phydev);

+	/*
+	 * The board may declare that the host SerDes is fixed at 10GBASE-R
+	 * and cannot follow the firmware's USXGMII-style line-rate changes
+	 * for sub-10G clients.  Re-provision those rates to 10GBASE-R (XFI)
+	 * + PAUSE rate matching so the line stays at 10G and the PHY
+	 * rate-adapts internally.
+	 */
+	if (of_property_read_bool(phydev->mdio.dev.of_node,
+				  "aquantia,host-10gbase-r-fixed")) {
+		static const u16 rate_cfg[] = {
+			VEND1_GLOBAL_CFG_100M, VEND1_GLOBAL_CFG_1G,
+			VEND1_GLOBAL_CFG_2_5G, VEND1_GLOBAL_CFG_5G,
+		};
+		int i;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(rate_cfg); i++) {
+			ret = phy_modify_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1, rate_cfg[i],
+					     VEND1_GLOBAL_CFG_SERDES_MODE |
+					     VEND1_GLOBAL_CFG_RATE_ADAPT,
+					     FIELD_PREP(VEND1_GLOBAL_CFG_SERDES_MODE,
+							VEND1_GLOBAL_CFG_SERDES_MODE_XFI) |
+					     FIELD_PREP(VEND1_GLOBAL_CFG_RATE_ADAPT,
+							VEND1_GLOBAL_CFG_RATE_ADAPT_PAUSE));
+			if (ret)
+				return ret;
+		}
+	}
+
 	ret = aqr107_set_downshift(phydev, MDIO_AN_VEND_PROV_DOWNSHIFT_DFLT);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
